#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:77
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of faac"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:80
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>faac</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:84
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./bootstrap                                &amp;&amp;\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr --disable-static &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:89
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This package does not come with a test suite. However, basic functionality "
"can be tested by encoding a sample WAV file (the sample file is installed by"
" the <xref linkend=\"alsa-utils\"/> package:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:94
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./frontend/faac -o Front_Left.mp4 "
"/usr/share/sounds/alsa/Front_Left.wav</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:97
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Then, decode the result using the <command>faad</command> program from the "
"<xref linkend=\"faad2\"/> package and play back the decoded file (requires "
"the <command>aplay</command> program from the <xref linkend=\"alsa-utils\"/>"
" package:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:103
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>faad Front_Left.mp4\n"
"aplay Front_Left.wav</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:107
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>aplay</command> should identify the file as <computeroutput>Signed "
"16 bit Little Endian, Rate 48000 Hz, Stereo</computeroutput>, and you should"
" hear the words <quote>front left.</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:113
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:116
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:121
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:143
#, xml-text
msgid "Other AAC encoders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:146
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The quality of <application>faac</application> is not up to par with the "
"best AAC encoders currently available. Also, it only supports AAC and not "
"High Efficiency AAC (also known as aacPlus), which provides better quality "
"at low bitrates by means of using the <quote>spectral band "
"replication</quote> technology. One example of an alternative program for "
"producing AAC and HE-AAC streams is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:168
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<ulink "
"url=\"https://portal.3gpp.org/desktopmodules/Specifications/SpecificationDetails.aspx?specificationId=1459\">3GPP"
" Enhanced aacPlus general audio codec</ulink>: available in the source form,"
" can encode only HE-AAC up to 48 kbps out of the box, but the maximum "
"bitrate can be changed by editing the tuning table in the "
"<filename>FloatFR_sbrenclib/src/sbr_main.c</filename> file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/faac.xml:179
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Note, however, that the iPod supports only the Low Complexity AAC profile, "
"which is the default in faac, but is completely unavailable in the 3GPP "
"encoder."
msgstr ""

